  "notes": [
    "Player 0 is out of position and has checked in the dark, so player 1 acts first. Node open is player 1's check or bet; node facing_bet is player 0's fold or call.",
    "Cases with a bet smaller than the pot have a unique equilibrium and pin both mixed frequencies, the Q bluff and the K call. At a bet equal to the pot the K call frequency is 0 and the Q bluff frequency is any value in [0, 1/2]; those facts are segment facts, and only the range level defense of 1/2 is pinned there.",
    "The pot sized numbers 04 section 6 states, bluffs are 1/3 of the betting range and the caller defends half of the bluff catchers, belong to the polar river toy game (case polar-river-pot-bet), where they are unique. In the AKQ game at a pot sized bet the same 1/3 is only the upper end of the segment, so gate G2 checks the AKQ frequencies at the two smaller bet sizes and the 04 numbers on the polar river case.",
    "Frequencies are compared within 0.5 percentage points, that is 0.005 in frequency units. The derivations are in validation/fixtures/README.md."
  ]
